            %p
          %p
          #HandednessOfMonadMorphism.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (handedness of the underlying natural transformation)
              %br/
              Beware that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwoCategoryOfMonads"}
              is oriented oppositely to what one might expect. This need not be so but is a possible choice, see
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Pumplün70"} Pumplün 1970 p 334
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Street72"} Street 1972 pp 158
            %p
              One issue is that the functor between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+categories"} Kleisli categories
              induced by a monad morphism goes in the direction
              %em opposite
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              as defined above (as generally for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
              along a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Frei69"} Frei 1969 p. 269
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Pumplün70"} Pumplün 1970 p 330
              %a{:href => "#BarrWells85"} Barr &amp; Wells 1985 §6.1
              and in our Exp.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransformationOfMonadsOnFixedCategory"}
              below) the association of monad morphisms to functors between Kleisli catgeories is contravariant (eg.
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Frei69"} Frei 1969, Thm. 2
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#BarrWells85"} Barr &amp; Wells 1985 Thm. 6.3
          %p
          #TransformationOfMonadsOnFixedCategory.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (transformation of monads on a fixed category)
              %br/
              This example is the simpler but important special case of the general Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwoCategoryOfMonads"}
              where the monads all act on the same fixed object – in particular the same category if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = Cat
              (stated in this form for instance in
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#BarrWells85"} Barr &amp; Wells 1985 §6.1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
              (where this is
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "monad+in+computer+science#Moggi89Abstract"} Moggi 1989 Def. 4.0.11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+types"} data
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            %p
              For a pair of monads
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi ret
                        %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi join
                        %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E}, ret^{\mathcal{E}}, join^{\mathcal{E}})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ret
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi join
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E}', ret^{\mathcal{E}'}, join^{\mathcal{E}'})
              on a fixed category
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
