          %p
          #ExtensionOfModalesAlongMonadTransformation.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              A monad transformation as in Exp.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransformationOfMonadsOnFixedCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariantly
              induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+categories"} Eilenberg-Moore categories
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monad"} modales
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#Frei69"}> Frei 1969, Thm. 2
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;:" do
                %a{:href => "#BarrWells85"} Barr &amp; Wells 1985 thm. 6.3
            %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/FunctorOnModalesFromMonadMorphism-230924.jpg", :width => "450px"}/
            %p
              Since this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
              is the identity on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+categories"} Kleisli categories
            %p#ExtensionOfFreeModalesAlsoIsomorphicMonadTransformation
