          %p
          #MonadTransformers.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (monad transfomers)
              %br/
              When monads are used to model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computational+effects"} computational effects
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+programming"} functional programming
              %em combine
              different effects, such that previous effects are subsumed among the newly combined effects. This is formalized by “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+transformers"}> monad transformers
              ” which are systems of morphisms of monads as in Exp.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransformationOfMonadsOnFixedCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+endofunctor"} pointed endofunctor
              on the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mnd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mnd
              of all monads.
          %p
          #IdentityMonadIsInitial.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in the category of monads on a fixed category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              (Exp.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransformationOfMonadsOnFixedCategory"}
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              We need to show that for every monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              there is a natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi trans
                      %mrow
