            %p
              which is the case by the unitality clause on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#Algebras Algebras/modules over a monad
          %p
            Given that a monad in a bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            is nothing but a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
            in a hom-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}(a,a)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            over this monoid: a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+for+a+monad"} module for a monad
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}(a,a)
            but can be in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}(b,a)
            (for left modules) or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}(a,c)
            (for right modules).
          %p
            In a
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+monad"} algebras over the monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            itself, such algebras with domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} 1
            are just algebras for a monad in the classical sense. Such algebras are a powerful tool to encode general algebraic structures; this is the topic of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+algebra"} universal algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
          %p
            Some monads arise from
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            is another special sort of monad in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %h2#properties Properties
          %div
            %h3#RelationBetweenAdjunctionsAndMonads Relation between adjunctions and monads
            %p
              There is a close relation between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"}> adjoint functors
              ) and
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#MonadInducedByAnAdjunction"} Monad induced by an adjunction
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#CategoryOfAdjunctionResolutionsOfAMonad"} Category of adjunction-resolutions of a monad
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#SemanticsStructureAdjunction"} Semantics-Structure adjunction
            %h4#MonadInducedByAnAdjunction Monad induced by an adjunction
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
              induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \circ L
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \circ R
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "monad#Huber61"}> Huber 1961, §4
              ; see eg.
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "monad#MacLane71"} MacLane 1971, §VI.1 (p 134)
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "monad#Borceux94"} Borceux 1994, vol. 2, prop. 4.2.1
            %p In detail:
            %p
            .num_prop
              %h6 Proposition
              %p
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi η
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C},\mathcal{D},F,U,\eta,\epsilon)
                be a pair of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
                ie
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \dashv U
                are adjoint functors where
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \rightarrow \mathcal{D}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon\mathcal{D} \rightarrow \mathcal{C}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{A}:A \rightarrow U(F(A))
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_{B} \colon F(U(B)) \rightarrow B
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \circ F
                    is a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
                    on
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi η
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                    and multiplication
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi ϵ
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo :
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\epsilon_{F(A)}):U(F(U(F(A)))) \rightarrow U(F(A))
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ U
                    is a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
                    on
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒟
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+a+comonad"} counit
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϵ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
                    and comultiplication
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi B
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
